GNU Emacs 31.1 language tests and the ERT framework they run on.
Release: GNU Emacs 31.1
Tarball: emacs-31.1.tar.gz from https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/emacs/
Tarball sha256: 3cad7fd1466c0e24867df8d2609da3ac75abc90d7c4c0175e410e9be46d4092a
Signature: emacs-31.1.tar.gz.sig, good signature from Sean Whitton
  (RSA key 9B917007AE030E36E4FC248B695B7AE4BF066240), checked 2026-10-17.
Files are copied verbatim from the tarball at the same relative paths; each
one's sha256 is in SHA256SUMS.  The 35 test files are the ones
tools/ai/gnu-language-conformance-progress.org measures; the *-resources
directories are the data files three of them read.
License: GPL-3.0-or-later, as in the tarball.
Support libraries (added 2026-10-18): lisp/emacs-lisp/{debug,backtrace,
find-func,ewoc}.el and lisp/help-mode.el, which ert.el requires, copied
verbatim from the same tarball because the library bundle the runner loads
no longer carries them.  tools/ai/gnu-tests-support.el appends this tree
to the end of load-path, so a provider already present wins.
